  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * @brief Q7 vector subtraction.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcA points to the first input vector
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcB points to the second input vector
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * @param[out]      *pDst points to the output vector
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * @param[in]       blockSize number of samples in each vector
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * @return none.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  *
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * \par
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * The function uses saturating arithmetic.
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  * Results outside of the allowable Q7 range [0x80 0x7F] will be saturated.
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c ****  */
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c **** 
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_sub_q7.c **** void arm_sub_q7(
